atlas optimization-proof

architecture optimization-proof
  canonical_name OptimizationProof
  owns ProofGate
  owns CompressionLedger
  owns CopyReceipt
  consumes CascadePlan
  consumes EvidenceGraph
  consumes RepresentationSelection
  publishes ProofGate
  publishes PromotionVerdict
  family optimization
  domain Optimization / Promotion gate
  layer governance
  semantic_question Is this materialization correct, and is it admissibly represented, and are those two questions being answered separately?
  purpose Prevent functionally correct but unnecessarily materialized implementations from being promoted. A semantic pass is necessary and not sufficient; a materialization must also prove identity, factoring, delta, borrowing, latent quality, cognitive role and reversibility.
  maturity architectural
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCompress/src/physical.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreCompress/tests/physical_compiler_test.sh records an executed zero-copy receipt and reports copy and hydration amplification separately from declared passport costs
  node_types ProofGate
  node_types CompressionLedger
  node_types CopyReceipt
  node_types PromotionVerdict
  edge_types gates
  edge_types measured_by
  invariant a semantic proof alone never promotes a materialization
  invariant a promotion verdict names which gate failed, never a single aggregate score
  invariant a ledger is a measurement of the machine doing its job, not a vanity metric
  invariant an unnecessary copy or materialization boundary on a hot path is an architectural failure, not a profiling curiosity
  invariant a compressed latent representation is admissible only with a measured retrieval-quality envelope
  invariant every lowering proves it can be lifted or thawed before it is promoted
  forbidden_inference a correct result -> a promotable implementation
  forbidden_inference a passing test suite -> an admissible representation
  forbidden_inference a smaller byte count -> a better representation
  forbidden_inference a ledger row existing -> a measurement having been taken
  interacts optimization-cascade
  interacts compression-law
  interacts cheap-cognition
  source_lineage Generation-10 optimization doctrine promotion, 2026-08-26

gate semantic
  question Is the thing represented correctly?
gate authority
  question Is relationship, data and effect ownership correct and exact?
gate physical
  question Are identical bodies deduplicated before any encoder runs?
gate compression
  question Was repeated structure factored into basis, binding and exception?
gate zero-copy
  question Did the hot path borrow where it could have borrowed?
gate delta
  question Are changes represented as changes rather than as new snapshots?
gate latent
  question Did the compressed representation retain measured retrieval quality?
gate cognitive
  question Did the cheap stage stay inside its admissible role?
gate query
  question Did the query avoid hydrating state it did not use?
gate reversibility
  question Can this lowering be lifted or thawed?

copy_receipt_field bytes_read
copy_receipt_field bytes_borrowed
copy_receipt_field bytes_copied
copy_receipt_field bytes_decompressed
copy_receipt_field bytes_reencoded
copy_receipt_field bytes_hydrated
copy_receipt_field allocations
copy_receipt_field serialize_count
copy_receipt_field deserialize_count
copy_receipt_field materialization_count
copy_receipt_field borrowed_boundaries
copy_receipt_field fused_boundaries
copy_receipt_field useful_bytes

ledger_section raw
  measure foreign bytes admitted
ledger_section identity
  measure unique bodies
  measure dedup ratio
  measure content-address hits
ledger_section exact
  measure normalized rows
  measure dictionary size
  measure packed-state bytes
  measure factorization ratio
ledger_section change
  measure full-state equivalent bytes
  measure actual delta bytes
ledger_section storage
  measure hot bytes
  measure warm bytes
  measure cold bytes
  measure compression ratio by domain dictionary
ledger_section latent
  measure baseline full-precision bytes
  measure selected representation bytes
  measure retrieval quality at k
  measure ranking stability
  measure residual energy
ledger_section cognitive
  measure cheap classifications performed
  measure escalation rate
  measure expensive operator invocations avoided
ledger_section execution
  measure copy amplification
  measure hydration amplification
  measure boundary-format parse count
  measure borrowed boundaries
  measure fused boundaries
ledger_section context
  measure prefill tokens avoided
  measure prepared state reused
  measure context cut bytes
ledger_section architectural
  measure motifs discovered
  measure capabilities lowered
  measure shared bases created
  measure explicit objects eliminated

representation_selection_protocol
  baseline full precision
  candidate half precision
  candidate integer quantization
  candidate product quantization
  candidate polar
  candidate polar plus residual
  candidate shared basis plus residual
  measure bytes
  measure recall at k
  measure ranking stability
  measure distance distortion
  measure query latency
  measure decode cost
  measure memory bandwidth
  measure residual energy
  measure temporal stability
  invariant selection is per subject family and measured, never a global default
  invariant this protocol applies to dense latent and model representations only and never to authority, permission or evidence lineage

interaction proof-gates-promotion
  source optimization-proof
  destination compression-law
  relation promotion_constraint
  preserves the separation between semantic correctness and representational admissibility
  drops any aggregate score that would let a failing gate be averaged away
  forbidden_inference an implementation passing every functional test -> that implementation being promotable
